Chapter: SheetChainTest
  cites Sheets chapter CellEval
  cites Sheets chapter CellGraph
  cites Sheets chapter CellStore
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 SHEET-7's milestone, and the register says why it is the first arm
 worth writing: a grid that renders is not evidence about anything the
 dependency graph touches. A chain of 1,000 cells, each naming the one
 above it, recalculated after an edit to the first.

 The chain is built with the LAST cell typed last, so entry order and
 derived order agree here on purpose: this arm measures the chain at
 size, and the arm that separates derived order from typing order is
 sheet-graph, where the sheet is three cells and the difference is
 readable.

 THE HEAP READING CARRIES ITS OWN CONTROL. `__heap-save` answers the
 allocator's pointer, and a difference between two reads is the bytes
 allocated between them. Two reads with NOTHING between them must differ
 by zero; the control line prints that difference, so an instrument that
 has started reporting something else fails visibly rather than making
 every other number on this page meaningless.

 The numbers are printed rather than compared against a recorded bound.
 A bound recorded today is a number nobody re-measures (L-COUNT), and
 the value of this line is the SHAPE: the cost of a chain of 1,000
 against the cost of one recalculation of it.

 TWO SIZES, because one number cannot say whether a cost is linear. The
 chain is built at 1,000 and at 4,000 and both build costs are printed:
 four times the cells for about four times the bytes is linear, and
 sixteen times is the quadratic this arm found and SHEET-8 removed.

Section: Body

  sc-len : Integer = 1000
  sc-big : Integer = 4000

  sc-build : Program, Integer, Integer -> Program
  sc-build (pg) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then pg
    else sc-build (graph-put pg i 0 ("=A" & show i & "+1")) (i + 1) n

  sc-last : Program, Results -> Text
  sc-last (pg) (rs) = eval-cell pg rs (sc-len - 1) 0

  sc-names : Program, Integer, Integer -> Text
  sc-names (pg) (r) (c) =
    let xs = graph-dependents pg r c
    in let n = list-length xs
    in if n == 0 then "(none)"
    else show n & ", first " & graph-name pg (list-at xs 0) & ", last " & graph-name pg (list-at xs (n - 1))

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let h0 = __heap-save
    in let h0b = __heap-save
    in let blk = sheet-new sc-len 2 64
    in let seed = sheet-set blk 0 0 5
    in let h1 = __heap-save
    in let pg = sc-build (graph-new blk) 1 sc-len
    in let h2 = __heap-save
    in let r1 = eval-run pg
    in let last1 = sc-last pg r1
    in let h3 = __heap-save
    in let edit = sheet-set blk 0 0 100
    in let r2 = eval-run pg
    in let last2 = sc-last pg r2
    in let h4 = __heap-save
    in let deps = sc-names pg 0 0
    in let h5 = __heap-save
    in let bigblk = sheet-new sc-big 2 64
    in let bigseed = sheet-set bigblk 0 0 5
    in let h6 = __heap-save
    in let bigpg = sc-build (graph-new bigblk) 1 sc-big
    in let h7 = __heap-save
    in let bigr = eval-run bigpg
    in let biglast = eval-cell bigpg bigr (sc-big - 1) 0
    in let h8 = __heap-save
    in act
      print-line-uni ("control: two heap reads with nothing between them differ by " & show (h0b - h0))
      print-line-uni ("a chain of " & show sc-len & " cells, A1 = 5, so A1000 = " & last1)
      print-line-uni ("edit A1 to 100 and recalculate: A1000 = " & last2)
      print-line-uni ("editing A1 recomputes " & deps)
      print-line-uni ("bytes to build and parse the chain: " & show (h2 - h1))
      print-line-uni ("bytes for one recalculation: " & show (h3 - h2))
      print-line-uni ("bytes for the second recalculation: " & show (h4 - h3))
      print-line-uni ("a chain of " & show sc-big & " cells, A4000 = " & biglast)
      print-line-uni ("bytes to build and parse " & show sc-big & ": " & show (h7 - h6))
      print-line-uni ("bytes to recalculate " & show sc-big & ": " & show (h8 - h7))
      print-line-uni ("build bytes per cell: " & show ((h2 - h1) / sc-len) & " at " & show sc-len & ", " & show ((h7 - h6) / sc-big) & " at " & show sc-big)
    end
